move-bringup (1.0.13-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: move-connman-shim — Python 3 daemon that owns the well-known
    name `net.connman` on the system bus and proxies MoveOriginal's WiFi
    UI calls to NetworkManager. Fixes the "WiFi screen shows nothing
    useful" symptom on the Move LCD: MoveOriginal was written against
    ConnMan and our Armbian image runs NetworkManager, so every
    `net.connman.Manager / .Technology / .Service` call was failing
    with ServiceUnknown and MoveOriginal's WiFi list / status was
    empty.
    The shim implements just enough of the ConnMan D-Bus surface to
    satisfy what MoveOriginal actually calls (captured via dbus-monitor
    on a live device): Manager.GetProperties / GetServices /
    GetTechnologies / RegisterAgent / UnregisterAgent;
    Technology[wifi].GetProperties / SetProperty / Scan;
    Service[N].GetProperties / Connect / Disconnect / SetProperty.
    Connect with PSK works end-to-end: shim calls MoveOriginal's agent
    (well-known name com.ableton.move, path captured from
    RegisterAgent) with Agent.RequestInput, then on response calls
    NM.AddAndActivateConnection. Service paths use stock ConnMan
    encoding (wifi_<bssid>_<ssidhex>_managed_<security>) so MoveOriginal
    parses them correctly.
    Signal-driven for low CPU — listens to NM Properties.PropertiesChanged
    + Device.Wireless.AccessPointAdded/Removed and re-emits the
    matching ConnMan signals (ServicesChanged, PropertyChanged). No
    polling. Per-AP property cache invalidated only on NM signal.
    Verified on hardware: 15 visible APs surfaced through GetServices
    with correct security tags (psk vs ieee8021x), signal strength,
    SSID; MoveLauncher registers its agent cleanly; resource use
    ~26 MB RSS / <1% CPU idle / ~1s CPU per restart.
  * Packaging:
    - python3-dbus-next added to Depends.
    - New file: /etc/dbus-1/system.d/move-connman-shim.conf granting
      root the net.connman bus name + allowing all users to call into
      our interfaces (MoveOriginal runs as ableton).
    - New file: /lib/systemd/system/move-connman-shim.service —
      Type=dbus, BusName=net.connman, ordered After=dbus +
      NetworkManager and Before=move-launcher so MoveOriginal sees us
      at its first net.connman call. MemoryMax=64M cap.
    - postinst enables + starts the new service.
  * The connman daemon itself is NOT installed; we provide just the
    D-Bus surface. Avoids the two-network-manager interference issue
    we hit with the connman-alongside-NM experiment.

 -- Move Port <move-port@localhost>  Fri, 16 May 2026 20:00:00 +0000

move-bringup (1.0.12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * setup-usb-network-gadget.sh: finally fix the USB-Ethernet NCM
    gadget. The 1.0.10 fixes (modules-load.d + idempotent stop) were
    necessary but not sufficient — the script's two `ln -sf "../...`
    invocations were silently failing because **configfs parses
    symlink targets to identify the referenced function/config and
    rejects any path with `..` traversal with ENOENT**, even though
    the path resolves correctly at the filesystem level. Verified on
    hardware (CM4 Rev 1.1, kernel 6.18.29-current-bcm2711): switching
    both ln calls from `-sf "../../functions/ncm.usb0" "configs/c.1/"`
    style to `-s "functions/ncm.usb0" "configs/c.1/"` style (paths
    relative to the gadget root, since cwd is g1/) makes ln succeed,
    UDC bind succeeds, /sys/class/udc/<udc> shows the bound gadget,
    and usb0 interface appears with the configured host/dev MACs:
        configfs-gadget.g1 gadget.0: HOST MAC 02:00:00:00:00:00
        configfs-gadget.g1 gadget.0: MAC 02:00:00:00:00:01
        dwc2 fe980000.usb: bound driver configfs-gadget.g1
    The path-form requirement matches what
    Documentation/usb/gadget_configfs.rst uses in its examples.
    Removed -f flag too — now redundant since stop() runs first as
    part of start() (per 1.0.10).

 -- Move Port <move-port@localhost>  Fri, 16 May 2026 19:00:00 +0000

move-bringup (1.0.11-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build fix: move rpi-eeprom + libraspberrypi-bin out of
    PACKAGE_LIST_BOARD (move.csc) and into customize-image.sh as
    best-effort installs (`apt install ... || true`). At the
    PACKAGE_LIST_BOARD dry-run stage, Armbian's chroot apt sources
    don't include the rpi-vendored archive that provides
    libraspberrypi-bin, so the dry-run fails with
        E: Package 'libraspberrypi-bin' has no installation candidate
    breaking the build. Installing later, in customize-image.sh after
    the chroot's sources are fully configured, is more reliable; the
    `|| true` keeps the build resilient if either package still can't
    be found (in which case BUILD.md §4c documents the manual install
    end users can do after first boot). No functional change for
    end users on a successful build.

