move-bringup (1.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ablspi-dkms: CRITICAL FIX — the driver now sets SPI_MODE_3
    (CPOL=1, CPHA=1) before spi_setup() in the probe path. The XMOS
    firmware samples MOSI on the falling SCLK edge and drives MISO on
    the rising edge; defaulting to SPI mode 0 produced "the bytes look
    right but every status byte is junk" garbage in both directions
    that even stock /opt/move/MoveLauncher could not decode ("Couldn't
    decode USB MIDI message {2, 14, 128, 128}"). Confirmed via
    objdump on the proprietary ablspi.ko:
        ablspi_probe+0x434:  orr  w2, w2, #0x3      ; mode |= 3
        ablspi_probe+0x438:  str  w2, [x20, #848]
        ablspi_probe+0x43c:  bl   spi_setup
    With this fix the XMOS replies cleanly to our SysEx batch and
    move-xmos-init confirms mode=1 (standaloneMode) on first boot.
  * move-xmos-init: poll the IN MIDI region on every frame during the
    wait phase and accumulate the reassembled stream — the XMOS only
    holds each reply slot for ~1 frame before overwriting it with the
    next event, so the old "wait then scan once" approach missed the
    burst of replies entirely.

 -- Move Port <move-port@localhost>  Wed, 13 May 2026 17:45:00 +0000

move-bringup (1.0.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * move-xmos-init: brought the replay byte sequence and ioctl pattern
    into exact alignment with a fresh stock-Move boot capture
    (capture-20260513-235610.bin, decoded with extended movesniff):
      - drop the spurious SEND_MESSAGE_AND_WAIT(0) kickoff; stock uses
        only SetSpeed + WAIT_AND_SEND_MESSAGE_WITH_SIZE, and our driver
        rejects size=0 as -EINVAL anyway.
      - prepend the 0xFF System Reset byte to the SysEx batch frame
        (stock writes this as the first OUT byte at +0.674s; without it,
        the XMOS appears to stay in raw-event mode instead of emitting
        USB-MIDI).
      - pack_midi() now recognises System Real-Time bytes (0xF8..0xFF)
        and encodes them with USB-MIDI CIN 0xF.
  * Ruled out the display region (OUT[80..255]) as the gating signal:
    in the stock capture it is zero through the entire init handshake
    and only starts seeing writes at +0.786s, well after mode=standalone
    was reported.

